#naming of ordinary artifacts is disallowed presumably because it's
the name that makes the game recognize it as an artifact; the devteam
wants to prevent players from creating artifacts by #naming (with
obvious exceptions).

#naming of unique items is allowed because they (especially the AoY)
are liable to be stolen and possibly replaced by (also named) fakes.
Allowing #naming here is a game balance issue. Or would you rather
climb the stairs on dlvl1, thinking you have the real Amulet, and find
that you've escaped the Dungeon with a fake?

I don't think these are bugs. I think they are thought-out game
features. At least you didn't call using the existing game features
"cheating."

